fmt writes through os.Stdout, a nil @File on bare-metal by design (os_baremetal.bn: "a bare-metal target has no standard output"), so the expected text is unattainable there — an environment limitation, not a codegen bug. The reflection substrate itself (the __typeinfo field table, reflect.TypeOf/DataOf) is architecture-neutral static data and works on native arm32; only fmt's stdout sink is missing. Hosted/VM-only test. Covers BOTH baremetal lanes: builder-comp_arm32_baremetal (this marker, LLVM) and builder-comp_native_arm32_baremetal (via OVERRIDE_MODE, run.sh).
